,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nachhiring language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nachhiring_language,"Grollmann (2018:2) reports that Nachiring is spoken in the villages of Aiselukharka, Hume, Para, Bakachol, Badel, Bangdel, Rakha, and Sumtel. It is not spoken anymore by ethnic Nachiring people living in Dharapani, Dipsun, and Dimma villages.",Nachiring,Sino-Tibetan
1,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"The soundtrack to Kundun, by Philip Glass, has helped to popularize Tibetan music. Foreign styles of popular music have also had a major impact within the Tibetan diaspora, where Indian ghazal and filmi are very popular and American rock has produced the India-based Rangzen Shonu.",Nachiring,Sino-Tibetan
2,"The traditional music of the Qiang, Pumi and Lisu ... - 資訊咖",https://inf.news/en/culture/f06f61414c45d182ef5689fbc0d80da1.html,"May 27, 2026 · The Sino-Tibetan language family is one of the largest and most dynamic language families in the world, with more than one billion speakers. What I want to introduce today is the traditional music of the Qiang, Pumi and Lisu people under the Sino-Tibetan language family.",Nachiring,Sino-Tibetan
3,Understanding the importance of Tibetan music - Tibet VistaYouTube MusicSINGING THE NATION: MODERN TIBETAN MUSIC AND NATIONAL IDENTITY1Tibetan Music & Audio — Stream & Download Traditional Music ...Nachhiring language - Wikipedia,https://www.tibettravel.org/tibetan-culture/understanding-the-importance-of-tibetan-music.html,"Tibet abides to current Asian pop culture very well and in no way is that a bad thing. They are well represented by their local bands and singers, such as Tsering Gyurmey, who has become one of the faces of modern sounds in Tibet. Songs celebrating Tibet’s traditions and past movements are commonplace for Tsering, and is well known and publicized f... See full list on tibettravel.org It is easy to identify at least five types of music exclusive of mainstream pop music (mentioned above). See full list on tibettravel.org Typically, Tibetan street and folk music is in acoustic form with the use of the Tungna, a four-stringed carved piece of wood topped with Yak skin. If accompanied, there could be a wide array of different percussion instruments used, such as cymbals, bells and drums. The beat doesn’t often change during one song so it is easy to follow along. Other... See full list on tibettravel.org New tibetan song 2023 Ngayi Monlam by Tenzin Dangsel ft. Lotsetan. བསྟ་འཛིན་དྭངས་གསལ་དང་བློ་ཚེ་བརྟན།. It ranges from songs sung in Tibetan and Chinese accompanied by Western musical instruments such as electronic synthesisers, and fusions of traditional Tibetan music with Indian or Western melodies, to subversive Tibetan rap. Listen to and download free Tibetan music, sacred chants, mantras, dharma teachings, folk songs, and oral histories. Stream rare recordings of traditional Tibetan instruments, monastic chanting, and contemporary Tibetan artists. Grollmann (2018:2) reports that Nachiring is spoken in the villages of Aiselukharka, Hume, Para, Bakachol, Badel, Bangdel, Rakha, and Sumtel. It is not spoken anymore by ethnic Nachiring people living in Dharapani, Dipsun, and Dimma villages.",Nachiring,Sino-Tibetan
